1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:04,730
A Claude Code session fills
its context window as it works.

2
00:00:05,120 --> 00:00:06,350
But with what?

3
00:00:08,950 --> 00:00:13,600
claude-watcher reads the session's
transcript, and splits the window by cause:

4
00:00:13,870 --> 00:00:18,280
tool results, tool definitions,
assistant output, and the rest.

5
00:00:20,450 --> 00:00:25,620
Each part opens into smaller ones:
per tool, per skill, per file.

6
00:00:25,910 --> 00:00:29,100
Down to the text itself,
as the model receives it.

7
00:00:30,650 --> 00:00:35,060
The total is the usage the
API reported, so it is exact.

8
00:00:35,350 --> 00:00:38,680
The split follows the growth
from one request to the next.

9
00:00:42,250 --> 00:00:45,760
Subagents get the same breakdown,
listed by their peak.

10
00:00:48,250 --> 00:00:53,820
It also lists every configured hook,
from every source, highest precedence first.

11
00:00:56,750 --> 00:01:00,300
All of it in the terminal,
kept current while the session runs.

12
00:01:06,300 --> 00:01:07,370
claude-watcher.

13
00:01:07,660 --> 00:01:09,410
See what fills your context.

